// Criterion: an empty kindexpr in **parameter position** is illegal -- parameters and return slots must declare a type.
//
// Negative case (4th state): layout is expected to fail with "parameter must declare a type".
// An empty kindexp is valid in only two places: bare `*` pointer target and empty mapexpr value `[int64]·`;
// both `* #x` and bare `#x` omit a required type and must not silently default to unconstrained.
//
// Why not test the **legacy syntax** `x:`: that would hit the migration diagnostic ("legacy `x:` is no longer accepted")
// first, testing grammar migration rather than rejection of an empty kindexpr in the **current grammar**.
//
// Historically this was a positive case asserting "`x:` means unconstrained" -- a rule superseded by the spec.
// Updating the criterion to reject empty parameter kindexprs enforces the current normative spec.
//
// Reference: 03-type-system/07-grammar-and-validity.kv (empty kindexp section),
//            05-langtype-signature-type-exprs.kv (parameters and return values must have types).
// Expected error: parameter must declare a type

rwfunc echo(* #x) -> (* #r) {
	*x -> *r
}

rwfunc test() -> () {
	println(echo(5))
	println(echo("hi"))
}
